      <abstract>
        <p>Burrowing has evolved repeatedly in marsupials, yet the genetic basis of digging behaviour is poorly understood. We compared 42 marsupial genomes and tested 1,204 genes for episodic positive selection on burrowing lineages. Three genes (<italic>BRW1</italic>, <italic>DIG2</italic> and <italic>CLAW3</italic>) showed convergent signatures of selection, and site-level models identified 25 codons under diversifying selection.</p>
      </abstract>
      <abstract abstract-type="summary">
        <title>Author summary</title>
        <p>Wombats, marsupial moles and bandicoots dig for a living. We asked whether the same genes changed each time burrowing evolved, and found three genes that did.</p>
      </abstract>
