  <body>
    <sec id="sec001" sec-type="intro">
      <title>Introduction</title>
      <p>Fossorial mammals share skeletal and behavioural adaptations for digging. Quokkason et al. (2015) [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref1">1</xref>] described burrowing-associated expression changes in wombat forelimbs, and Numbat and colleagues [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref2">2</xref>] later proposed that claw morphology evolves under strong selection<sup><xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref3">3</xref></sup>.</p>
      <p>Here we test whether the same genes are repeatedly targeted by selection across independent burrowing lineages, using the ratio of non-synonymous to synonymous substitution rates (d<sub>N</sub>/d<sub>S</sub>).</p>
    </sec>
    <sec id="sec002" sec-type="materials|methods">
      <title>Materials and methods</title>
      <sec id="sec003">
        <title>Sampling and <italic>ethics</italic></title>
        <p>All sampling procedures were approved by the University of Wombatia ethics board (protocol UW-17-42). Tissue requests can be sent to alice@quokka-lab.org. Samples were kept in the Nguyễn Lab’s freezer.</p>
      </sec>
      <sec id="sec004">
        <title>Selection analyses</title>
        <p>Gene-wide episodic selection was tested with a branch-site random-effects model in which the rate ratio <inline-formula><mml:math id="M1"><mml:mrow><mml:mi>ω</mml:mi><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mfrac><mml:msub><mml:mi>d</mml:mi><mml:mi>N</mml:mi></mml:msub><mml:msub><mml:mi>d</mml:mi><mml:mi>S</mml:mi></mml:msub></mml:mfrac></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula> varies across branches and sites:</p>
        <disp-formula id="eq1">
          <alternatives>
            <tex-math id="M2">\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}\begin{document}$$L(\theta) = \prod_{s} \sum_{k} p_k \, P(D_s \mid \omega_k)$$\end{document}</tex-math>
            <mml:math id="M3"><mml:mi>L</mml:mi></mml:math>
          </alternatives>
          <label>(1)</label>
        </disp-formula>
        <p>We used three complementary tests:</p>
        <list list-type="bullet">
          <list-item><p>BUSTED for gene-wide episodic selection;</p></list-item>
          <list-item><p>MEME for episodic site-level selection;</p></list-item>
          <list-item><p>RELAX for changes in selection intensity.</p></list-item>
        </list>
        <p>Detailed protocols are on our <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://www.quokka-lab.org/protocols">lab website</ext-link>.</p>
        <sec id="sec005">
          <title>Model comparison</title>
          <p>Nested models were compared with likelihood-ratio tests and P values were corrected with the Holm procedure.</p>
        </sec>
      </sec>
    </sec>
    <sec id="sec006" sec-type="results">
      <title>Results</title>
      <p>Of 1,204 genes tested, 31 showed evidence of episodic positive selection on at least one burrowing lineage, and three were selected on all four (<xref ref-type="table" rid="tab1">Table 1</xref>, <xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig1">Fig 1</xref>).</p>
